The original Li–Bulmer model provides an expression for the equilibrium probability of one of the two alleles under mutation-selection balance, P = 1/(1+βe−S), where S = 2 Ne  s with Ne being the effective population size and s being the selection coefficient for the target allele, and β is the mutation bias toward the other allele. A four-allele extension of this model was applied to the frequencies of four codons in a codon group (defined by the first two codon positions). The construction of this model can be understood by noting that the above equation represents a solution to the stationary distribution of a two-state Markov chain with transition matrix, P = \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
