Each ribosomal variant was evaluated using three biological replicates (n per variant = 3). Mean error rates (codon-specific or amino-acid-specific) were calculated by averaging across the three replicates per variant. Differences in overall translation-error rates, position-specific misreading, and minimum mutational distance (MMD) were evaluated by one-way ANOVA (two-sided). RMRs of preferred codons were tested against a null of 1 using a two-sided one-sample Wilcoxon signed-rank test across the 18 amino acids with synonymous codons. The standard error for each codon RMR was calculated by propagation of errors, which takes into account the standard error of each codon’s mean error rate (the RMR numerator) and the standard errors for the codons comprising the mean error rate for the synonymous codon family (the RMR denominator). Given that \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
